In article <10300@batcomputer.tn.cornell.edu> lenny@tcgould.tn.cornell.edu (Lenny Silver) writes:
>What about Arjuna's bow from the Mahabarata?  Didn't that have a name?

Yes. It was called the Gandiva, and was given to Arjuna by Agni, the God of
Fire. There are other named weapons from Indian Mythology. Shiva's bow is 
called the Pinaka, Vishnu's discus is called Sudarshana..There are many others.

Which brings up an interesting point. It would be interesting to see nethack
expanded to represent the mythologies of more countries. What do you guys 
think?

